meta {
  name: Ask for a download link
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/library/assets/{{assetId}}/link
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 409
}

docs {
  The read side of the upload, and it refuses for the same reason request 5
  does: nothing has been uploaded, so the asset is still pending and there is
  nothing to hand out a link to. "this asset has no uploaded object yet". A
  deleted asset gets the same status with a different sentence.

  Once an asset is ready this returns a presigned GET and its expiry. The link
  lasts five minutes, against fifteen for the upload, because a download link
  is the one that gets pasted into a chat window and forwarded -- it is a
  bearer credential for those bytes and nothing about it can be revoked.

  With no object store configured this is a 503 rather than a 409, for the same
  reason as request 5: there is no asset to ask about. See the folder docs.

  This is also why links are minted here and not folded into the asset body:
  reading an asset is something a listing page does dozens of times, and a
  signed URL in every one of those responses is a signed URL in every log.
}
